<!--
    kuna: a rustc ScalarPair return (Result/Option) loses its payload twice - the
    producer's second return register is deleted, and at the call site the payload
    register is a local the function never assigns.

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 call and prototype model, output-prototype.
    P0 assertion:      option rustabi off|auto|always  (default off).

    Source (rustc 1.x, -C opt-level=2 -C panic=abort -C relocation-model=static,
    x86-64, bytes verbatim below; both functions are #[inline(never)]):

        pub extern "Rust" fn prod(x: u32) -> Result<u32, u32> {
            if x > 10 { Ok(x * 2) } else { Err(x + 7) }
        }
        pub extern "C" fn cons(x: u32) -> u32 {
            match prod(x) { Ok(v) => v + 1, Err(e) => e + 100 }
        }

        prod:  lea (%rdi,%rdi,1),%ecx ; lea 0x7(%rdi),%edx ; xor %eax,%eax
               cmp $0xb,%edi ; setb %al ; cmovae %ecx,%edx ; ret
        cons:  push %rax ; call prod ; lea 0x1(%rdx),%esi ; lea 0x64(%rdx),%ecx
               test $0x1,%al ; cmove %esi,%ecx ; mov %ecx,%eax ; pop %rcx ; ret

    rustc returns the Result in the EAX:EDX pair - EAX the variant discriminant,
    EDX the payload - which is the storage the x86-64 cspec's join_dual_class
    output rule already describes, and kuna already recovers.

    The bug (pass 1, the default): the discriminant is materialized as
    `xor %eax,%eax; setb %al`, so RAX is a ONE-BIT logical value. Subvariable flow
    truncates the RETURN to that width, deleting the other register with it, and
    `prod` recovers as `bool prod(uint4)` with no payload at all. At the call site
    the second half of the recovered pair falls into the un-ported multi-trial
    branch of buildOutputFromTrials, so the CALL gets NO output and both registers
    render as locals nothing ever assigns - `v3 // edx` read twice, never written.

    The fix (pass 2, option rustabi always): the concatenation is recognized as a
    discriminant/payload pair from the observed writes and kept, and the call
    gains the join-space output the model asked for, with each half a SUBPIECE of
    it. `always` rather than `auto` because a bytechunk carries no `.comment`
    record for the source-language detection to read.

    The NEGATIVE half (scalar_callee / pair_shaped_reader, hand-written asm from
    tests fixture rust_clobber_pair_x86_64, verbatim below):

        scalar_callee:       movq %rdi,%rax ; addq $7,%rax ; ret
        pair_shaped_reader:  call scalar_callee ; lea 1(%rdx),%rcx
                             lea 100(%rdx),%rsi ; testb $1,%al
                             cmoveq %rsi,%rcx ; movq %rcx,%rax ; ret

    Byte for byte the caller-side shape of `cons` above - two used output trials,
    a byte-tested first register, a twice-read second one - but the callee
    PROVABLY never writes RDX. Nothing at the call site separates the two, so the
    call seam decodes the callee (`probe_callee_return_writes`) and refuses the
    pair. The reader must therefore render IDENTICALLY in both passes.
-->
